# Services of the PICO 4 Linux, run by /usr/libexec/pico4/pico4-init
# (busybox inittab syntax; see also /usr/libexec/pico4/svc).
# /init has already done all one-time setup before exec'ing init.
::respawn:/usr/libexec/pico4/svc udhcpd
::respawn:/usr/libexec/pico4/svc telnetd
::respawn:/usr/libexec/pico4/svc dropbear
::respawn:/usr/libexec/pico4/svc httpd
::respawn:/usr/libexec/pico4/svc serial
::respawn:/usr/libexec/pico4/svc usb-watch
::respawn:/usr/libexec/pico4/svc recovery-watch
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
# SIGQUIT (pico4-userspace switch): hand PID 1 to the installed system's systemd.
::restart:/usr/libexec/pico4/switch-userspace
::shutdown:/usr/libexec/pico4/svc shutdown
